/target
**/*.rs.bk
.DS_Store
/.superpowers/
/poc/claude-agent-sdk-bridge/node_modules/
/poc/claude-agent-sdk-bridge/capture.json
# Per-worktree scratch database (scripts/polyflare-service keeps a linked worktree off the
# shared live store).
/.polyflare-worktree/

# Browser-automation output. These are screenshots and accessibility dumps of a LIVE dashboard,
# so they carry account emails, internal account ids, the upstream account_id, and usage figures.
# They were committed by `git add -A` sweeping up a directory nothing was ignoring, and reached a
# public remote. Throwaway test output should never have been eligible for that in the first place.
/.playwright-mcp/
/playwright-report/
/test-results/
*.png.tmp

# Credential material and live data. None of this has ever been committed — every one of these
# lives in ~/.polyflare, outside the repo — and that is the point: this list exists so a stray
# `git add -A` from inside a data directory cannot make a first mistake, rather than to clean up
# after one.
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
auth.json
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.p12
id_rsa*
